                        "entry_id": "08c706a0-33a4-3d62-a362-38ba6623044c",
                        "glosses": [
                            "The chief, or highest-ranked physician of a prince, city or country, such as the Holy Roman Empire"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "e6e59fa9-104d-4580-b2ea-f110ae15f9ee",
                                "sense_id": "787eba58-8b54-3bc8-b0c6-11a7c77c54cd",
                                "text": "in his edition of Cicero's Oration for Archias , Lemgo , and Denmark , however , the dignity of Archiater still exists"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "84466e7e-a47e-4bcc-8fd9-c4da00264f92",
                                "sense_id": "787eba58-8b54-3bc8-b0c6-11a7c77c54cd",
                                "text": "He brought into private practice and made the best use of these methods of precision which he had employed as a teacher, soon became the archiater of New York, and was esteemed as much for his gentle qualities as for his professional ability"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
